  "limitations": [
    "Independent unbuilt source queue only: one real root commit, 12 original files comprising nine frozen source-directory files, two independent bounded-QA records and the payload manifest. No model, decoded video, new scene delivery or accepted reconstruction is present.",
    "All original paths, bytes and history are preserved without alteration. The source tree already has a files/ subdirectory: under the archive files/ container this remains files/files/. This preserves the real source tree rather than flattening or renaming its files. The producer payload manifest covers eleven files and excludes itself; the nested source manifest covers eight files and excludes itself. The consumer manifest includes all twelve files.",
    "Frozen metadata records official replay BV18C3d66E17 with event date 2026-08-02, two parts and decoded=false. Official clips BV1PKM967E6Z and BV1zcub6BEPH are recorded as material from that replay, published August 3 and August 7 respectively. This is archived identity evidence, not an external live-source revalidation by the archive worker, and not the separate June 6 offline anniversary concert.",
    "Five actual JPEG files are hashed and dimension-checked. Clip-2 and clip-3 are 1120x630 public covers; two YouTube covers are 1280x720 and the replay promotional cover is 720x540. All are non-native covers with unknown within-video times and no verified highest decoded quality. A larger version of the same clockwork image is not a second view; the promotional composite is not a room view.",
    "Clockwork-dial/gears and gold-pattern-platform/wood-stairs remain two separate local leads. Shared performance, clothing or replay identity does not establish one room. Neither has two independent structural views; occluded connections, clipped boundaries, hidden geometry, scale, mechanics and complete layout remain unknown. No modeling is initiated.",
    "Supplied independent QA is a limited visual precheck. Its 29-Issue text snapshot is neither the latest complete scene inventory nor a 29-scene pixel comparison. It reports actual comparison with an old banquet-hall crop and an observatory source image, while relevant old dark-railing, garden, terrace and piano-porch source pixels remain unavailable. Full deduplication and new-scene status are not established.",
    "The reviewed-pixels record contains four historical paths: two new covers are mapped and bound to their included frozen files; two old comparison images are external provenance records and are not included in this 12-file bundle or claimed independently reverified here. The original QA wording names clip-images.json; the included identity/image metadata is files/images.json. This historical wording is preserved verbatim, not silently rewritten.",
    "The recorded direct public HTML HTTP412 was stopped. Archived page text and image bytes do not establish video playback; no login transition, blocked request, old binary access, external search or alternative access path is attempted by this archive worker.",
    "A new independent archive/history pair is created from the latest verified archive tree solely to preserve old paths. Every preexisting remote ref and every prior path remains unchanged; only the new independent branches receive the source history, payload and verification receipt. The old denied source-screening-increment receipt stays paused.",
    "Only official Library reception, ordinary Git and completeness checks are performed. No modeling/rendering, production-tree writes, credentials copied, security settings changed, LFS, force push, deleted history, main changes, Issues or PRs. Library version 0 remains retained for parent consumption confirmation; no Space deletion or permanent attachment is performed."
  ],
